{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Legally integrate NHS and School support for children with ADHD and SEND",
        "additional_details": "We are concerned that parents of neurodivergent children are being pushed to breaking point by having to fight separate state systems. We feel parents are forced into a constant cycle of chasing teachers to justify our children\u2019s needs, while simultaneously being left in complete limbo by NHS and Integrated Care Board (ICB) funding bottlenecks. The current system treats health and education as completely isolated silos, placing the entire burden of communication, advocacy, and stress onto exhausted families. We believe this is unacceptable.",
        "background": "Formally link NHS and school SEN teams so medical updates, medication issues and funding delays are shared automatically. Require ICBs to resolve care delays within set timeframes and ensure schools support children awaiting NHS care, without parents constantly chasing services.",
